<Legal
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="revenuedot.app and the RevenueDot dashboard set three analytics cookies outside Europe and none in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland. The dashboard also uses one strictly necessary session cookie."
  path="/legal/cookies"
  updated="2026-10-02"
  lede="Outside the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, our website and dashboard set three first-party analytics cookies from DataFast. Inside those regions they set none, so there is no cookie banner. The dashboard also uses one cookie to keep you signed in."
>
  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>revenuedot.app and app.revenuedot.app use DataFast (datafa.st) to count visits, see which channel brought a visitor, and credit a paid plan to that channel. Visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, as Cloudflare detects them, get DataFast's cookieless script: it sets no cookies and uses no local storage for tracking. Everyone else gets these first-party cookies, set on revenuedot.app and its subdomains:</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th><th scope="col">Type</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="num-cell">datafast_visitor_id</td><td>A random id that recognizes a returning browser, so a signup and a payment can be credited to the channel of the first visit.</td><td>365 days</td><td>Analytics, first party</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="num-cell">datafast_session_id</td><td>A random id for the current visit.</td><td>30 minutes</td><td>Analytics, first party</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="num-cell">datafast_visitor_session_count</td><td>How many visits this browser has made.</td><td>365 days</td><td>Analytics, first party</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>When you sign in or send the contact-sales form, your email address and name are sent to DataFast so the visit, the signup and the payment show as one profile. See the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy policy</a>. To stop the cookies, block datafa.st or clear the cookies for revenuedot.app.</p>

  <h2>The RevenueDot dashboard</h2>
  <p>The dashboard, in RevenueDot Cloud and in self-hosted installs, sets one strictly necessary cookie:</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th><th scope="col">Type</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="num-cell">rd_session</td><td>Keeps you signed in. HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure over HTTPS.</td><td>30 days, or until you sign out</td><td>Strictly necessary, first party</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Strictly necessary cookies do not need consent under the ePrivacy rules, because the dashboard cannot sign you in without it. The dashboard also keeps two preferences in your browser's local storage, your theme and whether the setup checklist is hidden; they never leave your device.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.legal}`}>{SITE.email.legal}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
